    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "validation: check the sigops limit before staging a transaction",
    "user": {
      "login": "fametrano",
      "id": 3296421,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTY0MjE=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3296421?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/fametrano",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "A transaction over the standard sigops limit is added to the mempool's staging area before that limit is checked. With a large `-bytespersigop`, its sigop-adjusted weight does not fit in the `int32_t` size that `TxGraph` uses, so `Assume(feerate.size > 0)` in `TxGraphImpl::AddTransaction` fails and a debug build aborts. A release build rejects the transaction as before.\n\nI moved the sigops check to right after the sigops are counted, before staging. The new case in `mempool_sigoplimit.py` sends a transaction with 16001 sigops to a node run with `-bytespersigop=134210`. On master, a debug build of the node aborts on that `Assume`. With this change, the transaction is rejected with `bad-txns-too-many-sigops`. This does not bound `-bytespersigop` itself: a large enough value still overflows the size of a transaction within the limit.\n",
